Use case: identity-preserve. Asset type: IN-BETWEEN animation drawings inserted between six existing consecutive frames.
Input image1 is the authoritative SIX-FRAME motion strip for the same character. Input image2 is the approved original identity. Match image1's exact same face, costume, palette, weapons, brown linework, camera, body scale and feet. Do not redesign or reinterpret.
Draw SIX NEW interpolation frames for the kim / encourage gesture: Her empty left hand becomes an encouraging fist beside her shoulder, smiling brightly with an open mouth. Keep the right hand holding her original sword lowered diagonally, as in reference1.
The six cells of reference1 read top row left to right (A0,A1,A2), then bottom row left to right (A3,A4,A5). The new output cells must be:
B0 exactly HALFWAY between A0 and A1, with only half the wrist/elbow/facial change;
B1 halfway between A1 and A2;
B2 halfway between A2 and A3;
B3 halfway between A3 and A4;
B4 halfway between A4 and A5;
B5 the A5 ending pose settling very subtly, hair/ribbons relax by a few pixels, torso/boots fixed.
These new B drawings will be interleaved A0 B0 A1 B1 A2 B2 A3 B3 A4 B4 A5 B5, so every B must genuinely bridge its two neighbors, NOT be a new independent pose or repeat an endpoint. Natural anatomical elbow/wrist paths, subtle eyelid and mouth movement; no extra limbs. Keep head shape/center, torso, legs, boot positions, sword/shield and anatomy fixed except exactly the moving parts in reference1. Original character identity is critical.
Output one SQUARE transparent RGBA sheet, exactly 3 COLUMNS x 2 ROWS in this reading order. Cell aspect2:3. Full-body figures same scale and fixed camera. Complete silhouettes including every hair tip, sword, shield, cape and boot inside their own cells; LARGE fully transparent margins/gutters around all six figures. No words, borders, frame numbers, scenery, shadow floor or glow. True alpha background. Highest practical detail, no blur. Render smooth incremental 2D anime drawings, not whole-figure translations or zooms.

